        "orario": "12:22",
        "timestamp": 1780741357,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Parliamentary elections mark 'historical moment' for Armenia, expert says Asia / Pacific Issued on: 06/06/2026 - 12:22 Armenia's upcoming parliamentary elections, which could reshape the country's ties with Russia and the West, mark a \"historic moment\" for the country, according to Ulrich Schmid, Professor of Eastern European Studies at the University of St Gallen. Incumbent Prime Minister Nikol Pashinyan is seeking to normalise relations with Turkey and neighbouring Azerbaijan, with which Armenia has been locked in conflict for decades. Armenia prepares for vote amid shifting relations with Russia and the West 06/06/2026 Asia / Pacific Thailand: Sexual abuse scandal inside family business empire forces public reckoning 05/06/2026 Asia / Pacific Rescuers pull four villagers trapped in a flooded cave during ten days 31/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Trapped in a cave for a week: Rescuers in Laos evacuate first of five villagers 30/05/2026 Asia / Pacific 5 people trapped in Laos cave found alive, 2 still missing 27/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Starbucks faces South Korean backlash following campaign echoing 1987 massacre 26/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Marco Rubio visits India as US and India seek to ease trade tensions 25/05/2026 Americas China prepares for future Moon mission with new crew launch 25/05/2026 Asia / Pacific India’s “Cockroach Janta Party” goes viral as Gen Z movement grows 25/05/2026 Asia / Pacific"
